### ========== Rifd — full demo walkthrough (IntelliJ HTTP client) ==========
### security.enabled=false -> no token needed. Seed ids: staff 1 = operator1, 3 = supervisor1.

### 0) Reset (safe to run any time)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/simulation/reset

### 1) Start the 40-alert scenario (speed 2 = ~1 minute)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/simulation/start?speed=2

### 1b) Progress
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/simulation/status

### 2) Stats -> totalAlerts 40, mergedAlerts 37, openIncidents 3, bySeverity HIGH 1 / MEDIUM 1 / LOW 1
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/dashboard/stats

### 3) Incidents (HIGH first)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents

### 4) Recommendation of the crowd incident (INC-0001 -> id 1)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/1/recommendations

### 5) Preview who would go (2 certified crowd supervisors + 1 escort assistant)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/1/candidates

### 6) Operator accepts -> automatic assignment (use the recommendation id from step 4)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/recommendations/1/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actorStaffId": 1 }

### 7) Tasks of the incident
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/1/tasks

### 8) Field staff accepts and starts walking (task id from step 7) -> staff moves on the map
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tasks/1/accept

###
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tasks/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "EN_ROUTE" }

### 9) A staff member rejects -> next nearest is assigned automatically
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tasks/2/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Already handling a lost child at Pavilion A" }

### 10) Accessibility: elevator out -> route DISRUPTED + alternative + bilingual message
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/accessibility/assets

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/accessibility/routes

### route 1 = Main Plaza -> Pavilion B (Elevator B2)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/accessibility/routes/1/alternative

### 11) Notifications of the accessibility team
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/notifications?specialty=ACCESSIBILITY&unread=true

### 12) Activity log: AI / HUMAN / SYSTEM for each decision
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/1/activity

### 13) Close the elevator incident (id 2) -> asset OPERATIONAL, route ACTIVE, staff released
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/2/resolve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resolutionNotes": "Elevator restarted by technician", "actualSeverity": "MEDIUM", "actorStaffId": 1 }

### 14) Manual assignment (operator picks a specific person)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "incidentId": 3, "staffId": 25, "notes": "Bring the wet-floor sign", "actorStaffId": 1 }

### 15) Plan B for the demo: break an asset by hand (supervisor)
###     NOTE: closing the incident will NOT bring it back (set by a human) -> run 15b after closing
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/accessibility/assets/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "OUT_OF_SERVICE", "actorStaffId": 3 }

### 15b) Bring the asset back by hand (after closing the incident)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/accessibility/assets/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "OPERATIONAL", "actorStaffId": 3 }

### 16) Login (when security.enabled=true) -> use the token as: Authorization: Bearer <token>
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "operator1", "password": "demo123" }

### Staff / playbooks
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/staff?role=FIELD&status=AVAILABLE

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/playbooks?active=true


### ========== Logic-review fixes (handoff section 13.6) ==========
### Run 0 (reset) + 1 (start) first. Ids below assume a fresh reset: INC-0001 = 1 (crowd), 2 (elevator), 3 (spill).

### 17) Operator cancels a task (any open state) -> CANCELLED, staff AVAILABLE, TASK_CANCELLED notification,
###     incident back to OPEN + ESCALATED if nobody is left on it (from ASSIGNED or IN_PROGRESS,
###     unless another task is already DONE)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tasks/1/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Severity lowered, one supervisor is enough", "actorStaffId": 1 }

### 18) Fresh recommendation on demand (after a reject / manual assignment / not enough staff)
###     -> old PENDING = SUPERSEDED, new PENDING with only the missing staff count
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/1/recommendations/regenerate

### 19) One alert
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/alerts/1

### 20) Dismiss a wrongly merged alert -> DISMISSED, alertCount - 1, ALERT_UPDATED on /topic/alerts, stats updated
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/alerts/5/dismiss
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Sensor test message, not a real event", "actorStaffId": 1 }

### 21) Who am I (needs security.enabled=true + the token from step 16). Without a token -> 400 "Not logged in"
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <paste-token-here>

### 22) LOCK TEST: run this WHILE the simulation is still sending alerts (right after step 1)
###     -> INC-0001 must stay RESOLVED; later crowd alerts open a NEW incident (INC-0004)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/1/resolve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resolutionNotes": "Lock test", "actorStaffId": 1 }

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/1

### 23) Long rejection reason (> 255 chars) -> must succeed (column is 500 now)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tasks/2/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Staff member is assisting another urgent case and cannot leave the current position. Staff member is assisting another urgent case and cannot leave the current position. Staff member is assisting another urgent case and cannot leave the current position. Staff member is assisting another urgent case and cannot leave the current position." }

### 24) ACCEPTED -> DONE directly -> incident IN_PROGRESS + "All tasks are done" in the activity log
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tasks/3/accept

###
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tasks/3/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "DONE" }

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/3/activity

### 25) Manual BUSY is not allowed -> 400 "BUSY is set by tasks only"
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/staff/25/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "BUSY" }

### 26) MAINTENANCE stays: reset (0) -> put Elevator B2 (asset 1) in MAINTENANCE -> start (1)
###     -> resolve the elevator incident (13) -> asset 1 must still be MAINTENANCE
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/v1/accessibility/assets/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "MAINTENANCE", "actorStaffId": 3 }

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/accessibility/assets

### Reopen a closed incident (operator)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/2/reopen
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Closed by mistake, elevator still broken", "actorStaffId": 1 }

### Reopen an open incident -> 400 "Incident is not closed"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/2/reopen
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "test", "actorStaffId": 1 }

### Field staff closing an incident -> 400 "Only operators and supervisors can do this"
### (replace 5 with the id of a FIELD staff member)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/1/resolve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resolutionNotes": "test", "actorStaffId": 5 }